-- CONTROL for s3-nested-obligation-two-levels (#323). Same interface, same depth
-- (`List (List (List Int))`), the overlapping `impl Tag (List Int)` REMOVED.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived): only `Tag (List a)` matches at each of the three
-- levels, bottoming out at `Tag Int`: 10 + 10 + 10 + 1 => 31.
--
-- OBSERVED: check/run/build all ACCEPT and all print 31. CONFORMANT.
--
-- Why this row is load-bearing: without it, s3-nested-obligation-two-levels'
-- eval panic could be read as "eval cannot do depth-3 nesting at all", which is
-- FALSE and would send a fixer at the wrong subsystem. This control proves the
-- run path handles depth-3 recursive context discharge fine, and that #323's
-- trigger is specifically the presence of a strictly-more-specific overlapping
-- instance below the recursion.
interface Tag a where
  tag : a -> Int

impl Tag Int where
  tag _ = 1

impl Tag (List a) requires Tag a where
  tag xs = match xs
    (y :: _) => 10 + tag y
    [] => 10

main = println (tag ([[[1]]] : List (List (List Int))))
